PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L07U6.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":7,"cefr":"B1+","unit":6,"theme":"Arts and Creativity","essential_question":"Why do people create art?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS1","title":"I Had My Calligraphy Framed: Causative have / get something done","objectives":["Students will be able to talk about services that other people do for them with have/get + object + past participle.","Students will be able to use the causative in different tenses and with have + person + base verb.","I can say \"I had my calligraphy framed\" and \"I'm getting my phone repaired.\"","I can say \"I had my brother take the photos.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من التحدث عن الخدمات التي يقدّمها الآخرون لهم بـ have/get + المفعول + التصريف الثالث.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام صيغة السببية في أزمنة مختلفة ومع have + الشخص + المصدر.","أستطيع أن أقول I had my calligraphy framed وI'm getting my phone repaired.","أستطيع أن أقول I had my brother take the photos."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"exhibition","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɛksəˈbɪʃən/","definition":"a public show of art or other interesting things","arabic":"معرض","example":"The school art exhibition opens on Thursday.","image_id":"GV-L07-U6-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS1-W01"},{"word":"calligraphy","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kəˈlɪɡrəfi/","definition":"the art of beautiful handwriting","arabic":"فن الخط","example":"Arabic calligraphy decorates many mosques.","image_id":"GV-L07-U6-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS1-W02"},{"word":"sculpture","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈskʌlptʃɚ/","definition":"a piece of art made by shaping stone, wood, metal or clay","arabic":"منحوتة / مجسّم","example":"There's a huge sculpture of a falcon in the square.","image_id":"GV-L07-U6-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS1-W03"},{"word":"mosaic","pos":"noun","ipa":"/moʊˈzeɪɪk/","definition":"a picture made from many small pieces of colored stone, glass or tile","arabic":"فسيفساء","example":"The mosque floor has a beautiful blue mosaic.","image_id":"GV-L07-U6-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"We use the causative when someone else does a job or service for us: I had my pieces framed. (Mr. Hasan framed them – I didn't.) Form: have + object + past participle. get + object + past participle means the same but is more informal: I got the poster printed.\nChange the tense of have / get to show the time: I'm having it repaired this week. I had it repaired last week. I'll get it repaired tomorrow. I've had it repaired twice. We can add by + person: I'm going to have the lights checked by the school technician.\nhave + person + base verb means we ask or arrange for a person to do something: I had my brother take photos. We also use have something done for bad experiences: My uncle had his car stolen. Watch the word order: (not: I had framed my pieces) (= past perfect: I did it myself!).\nhave / get + object + past participle\ntense goes on have / get: am having, had, will get, have had\nhave + person + base verb (arrange for someone to do it)\norder matters: had my pieces framed ≠ had framed my pieces","examples":["We had our house painted before Eid.","Lina gets her eyes tested every year.","I'm having my thobe shortened at the tailor's.","The museum is having its old roof repaired.","Dad had the car washed at the gas station.","I'll get my photos printed for the school magazine.","Saad had his phone stolen on the bus.","The teacher had the students clean their brushes."],"common_errors":["✗ I cut my hair at the barber's. (the barber did it) → ✓ I had my hair cut at the barber's. (Someone else did it → causative.)","✗ I had framed my pictures at the shop. → ✓ I had my pictures framed at the shop. (Object before the past participle.)","✗ I'm having my phone repair. → ✓ I'm having my phone repaired. (Past participle.)","✗ I had my brother to take the photos. → ✓ I had my brother take the photos. (have + person + base verb (no to).)"],"arabic":"صيغة السببية: نستخدمها عندما يقوم شخص آخر بعمل أو خدمة لنا: I had my pieces framed (جعلتُ شخصًا يؤطّر لوحاتي).\nالتركيب: have / get + المفعول + التصريف الثالث، وget أقل رسمية.\nالزمن يظهر على have / get: I'm having it repaired / I had it repaired / I'll get it repaired.\nhave + الشخص + المصدر: I had my brother take photos. وتُستخدم أيضًا للتجارب السيئة: He had his car stolen."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “I Had My Calligraphy Framed: Causative have / get something done”. Let’s learn causative have / get + object + past participle (a service someone else does for us); have + person + base verb; tenses of the causative; bad experiences (had my phone stolen) together.","on_screen":"GV-L07-U6-LS1 | I Had My Calligraphy Framed: Causative have / get something done","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Getting Ready for the Exhibition – Faisal”: Next month, our school is holding its first art exhibition, and I'm getting everything ready for my Arabic calligraphy display. I can write the calligraphy myself, but I can't do everything alone. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Next month, our school is holding its first art exhibition, and I'm getting everything ready for my Arabic calligraphy display. I can write the calligraphy myself, but I can't do everything alone.","visual":"Image GV-L07-U6-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"We use the causative when someone else does a job or service for us: I had my pieces framed. (Mr. Hasan framed them – I didn't.) Form: have + object + past participle. get + object + past participle means the same but is more informal: I got the poster printed. Change the tense of have / get to show the time: I'm having it repaired this week. I had it repaired last week. I'll get it repaired tomorrow. I've had it repaired twice. We can add by + person: I'm going to have the lights checked by the school technician.","on_screen":"have / get + object + past participle • tense goes on have / get: am having, had, will get, have had • have + person + base verb (arrange for someone to do it)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. We had our house painted before Eid. Lina gets her eyes tested every year. I'm having my thobe shortened at the tailor's.","on_screen":"We had our house painted before Eid. / Lina gets her eyes tested every year. / I'm having my thobe shortened at the tailor's.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I cut my hair at the barber's. (the barber did it).” That’s not right. We say: “I had my hair cut at the barber's.” Someone else did it → causative.","on_screen":"✗ I cut my hair at the barber's. (the barber did it)   ✓ I had my hair cut at the barber's.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"I had my pieces framed.\" Did I frame them? … Think! … No – the framer did. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I had my calligraphy framed\" and \"I'm getting my phone repaired.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"I had my calligraphy framed\" and \"I'm getting my phone repaired.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: causative have / get + object + past participle (a service someone else does for us); have + person + base verb; tenses of the causative; bad experiences (had my phone stolen).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","صيغة السببية: نستخدمها عندما يقوم شخص آخر بعمل أو خدمة لنا: I had my pieces framed (جعلتُ شخصًا يؤطّر لوحاتي).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I cut my hair at the barber's. (the barber did it) — الصحيح: I had my hair cut at the barber's.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول I had my calligraphy framed وI'm getting my phone repaired."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Getting Ready for the Exhibition – Faisal","body":"Next month, our school is holding its first art exhibition, and I'm getting everything ready for my Arabic calligraphy display. I can write the calligraphy myself, but I can't do everything alone.\nLast week, I had my best pieces framed at a small shop in the old souq. The framer, Mr. Hasan, has worked there for forty years, and his frames are beautiful. Yesterday, I got the large poster printed at a print shop near the school because our printer is too small.\nMy brother, Ziyad, is a photographer, so I had him take photos of each piece for the online catalog. He's very patient – he took more than two hundred photos!\nThere's one problem: one of my frames was cracked when I picked it up. I'm having it repaired this week. I also need to get my name engraved on a small brass plate for each frame.\nOn the day of the exhibition, I'm going to have the lights checked by the school technician, because good lighting makes calligraphy shine.\nI'm nervous, but I'm also excited. My grandfather, who taught me my first letters, is coming to see the show!","word_count":192,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"I can't frame pictures myself, so I ___ my calligraphy framed at a shop.","options":["had","made","let","did"],"answer":"had","explanation":"have + object + past participle.","explanation_ar":"have + المفعول + التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"We got our class photo ___ yesterday.","options":["print","printed","printing","to print"],"answer":"printed","explanation":"get + object + past participle (informal).","explanation_ar":"get للتعبير غير الرسمي."},{"q":"My tablet screen is cracked. I'm ___ it repaired this week.","options":["letting","doing","making","having"],"answer":"having","explanation":"Change the tense of have/get.","explanation_ar":"زمن have/get."},{"q":"Faisal had his brother ___ photos of every painting.","options":["take","to take","taking","taken"],"answer":"take","explanation":"have + person + base verb.","explanation_ar":"have + الشخص + المصدر."},{"q":"Someone at the library scanned Lina's drawings for her. Which sentence says this?","options":["Lina had her drawings scan at the library.","Lina had scanned her drawings at the library.","Lina had her drawings scanned at the library.","Lina scanned her drawings at the library."],"answer":"Lina had her drawings scanned at the library.","explanation":"Object before the past participle.","explanation_ar":"المفعول قبل التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"My uncle ___ his car stolen last month. It was terrible!","options":["did","made","let","had"],"answer":"had","explanation":"have + object + past participle.","explanation_ar":"have + المفعول + التصريف الثالث."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with the causative. Word bank: are having it restored, got my bike fixed, will have her artwork displayed","items":[{"q":"The old museum needs work, so they ______ (have / it / restore) this year.","options":[],"answer":"are having it restored","explanation":"Change the tense of have/get.","explanation_ar":"زمن have/get."},{"q":"I ______ (get / my bike / fix) at the shop near the mosque.","options":[],"answer":"got my bike fixed","explanation":"get + object + past participle (informal).","explanation_ar":"get للتعبير غير الرسمي."},{"q":"Next week, Noura ______ (have / her artwork / display) in the library.","options":[],"answer":"will have her artwork displayed","explanation":"Change the tense of have/get.","explanation_ar":"زمن have/get."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS1-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Rewrite with have/get something done.","items":[{"q":"A photographer took our family photo. (We… / have)  (causative)","options":[],"answer":"We had our family photo taken by a photographer.","explanation":"have + object + past participle.","explanation_ar":"have + المفعول + التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"Someone is painting our house this week. (We… / get)  (causative)","options":[],"answer":"We're getting our house painted this week.","explanation":"get + object + past participle (informal).","explanation_ar":"get للتعبير غير الرسمي."},{"q":"The tailor will shorten my thobe tomorrow. (I… / have)  (causative)","options":[],"answer":"I'll have my thobe shortened tomorrow.","explanation":"Change the tense of have/get.","explanation_ar":"زمن have/get."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Talk about services.","items":[{"q":"Something you have done regularly (hair, eyes, teeth): ___","options":[],"answer":"I have my hair cut every month.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses causative have / get + object + past participle (a service someone else does for us); have + person + base verb; tenses of the causative; bad experiences (had my phone stolen) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something your family had done at home recently: ___","options":[],"answer":"We had the air conditioner serviced last week.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses causative have / get + object + past participle (a service someone else does for us); have + person + base verb; tenses of the causative; bad experiences (had my phone stolen) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something you're going to get done before the next holiday: ___","options":[],"answer":"I'm going to get my bike repaired before the holiday.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses causative have / get + object + past participle (a service someone else does for us); have + person + base verb; tenses of the causative; bad experiences (had my phone stolen) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something you would never have done for you: ___","options":[],"answer":"I would never have my homework done by someone else!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses causative have / get + object + past participle (a service someone else does for us); have + person + base verb; tenses of the causative; bad experiences (had my phone stolen) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Someone you had do something for you: ___","options":[],"answer":"I had my sister check my English essay.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses causative have / get + object + past participle (a service someone else does for us); have + person + base verb; tenses of the causative; bad experiences (had my phone stolen) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Prepare an exhibition.","items":[{"q":"You are organizing a class art show. Write 3 things you'll have or get done.","options":[],"answer":"We'll have the posters printed. We'll get the paintings framed. We'll have the hall cleaned.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses causative have / get + object + past participle (a service someone else does for us); have + person + base verb; tenses of the causative; bad experiences (had my phone stolen) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 things you'll do yourselves.","options":[],"answer":"We'll write the labels ourselves. We'll hang the paintings ourselves.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses causative have / get + object + past participle (a service someone else does for us); have + person + base verb; tenses of the causative; bad experiences (had my phone stolen) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 1 sentence with have + person + base verb.","options":[],"answer":"We'll have Mr. Khalid check the lights.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses causative have / get + object + past participle (a service someone else does for us); have + person + base verb; tenses of the causative; bad experiences (had my phone stolen) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Grammar Hot Seat","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["One student from each team sits in the hot seat facing the class.","The teacher shows a cue card behind the student; the team gives a clue using causative have / get + object + past participle (a service someone else does for us); have + person + base verb; tenses of the causative; bad experiences (had my phone stolen) without saying the word.","The student in the hot seat guesses the cue word within 30 seconds.","Teams score 1 point for a correct guess and 1 point for a correct clue sentence. Rotate seats."],"data":[{"label":"have it framed"},{"label":"get it printed"},{"label":"had my bike repaired"},{"label":"I'm having… done"},{"label":"make me practice"},{"label":"let us choose"},{"label":"allow us to use"},{"label":"was made to wait"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"I don't cut my own hair. I ___ it cut at the barber's every month.","options":["do","have","make","let"],"answer":"have","explanation":"have + object + past participle.","explanation_ar":"have + المفعول + التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"We ___ our carpets cleaned before Ramadan.","options":["let","did","made","got"],"answer":"got","explanation":"get + object + past participle (informal).","explanation_ar":"get للتعبير غير الرسمي."},{"q":"Lina's glasses are broken. She's ___ them fixed today.","options":["doing","making","getting","letting"],"answer":"getting","explanation":"Change the tense of have/get.","explanation_ar":"زمن have/get."},{"q":"The principal had the students ___ their classroom.","options":["to decorate","decorated","decorate","decorating"],"answer":"decorate","explanation":"have + person + base verb.","explanation_ar":"have + الشخص + المصدر."},{"q":"","options":["We had the walls painted blue.","We had the walls paint blue.","We had the walls to be painted blue.","We had painted the walls blue by a painter."],"answer":"We had the walls painted blue.","explanation":"Object before the past participle.","explanation_ar":"المفعول قبل التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"Where do you usually ___ your shoes repaired?","options":["make","have","let","do"],"answer":"have","explanation":"have + object + past participle.","explanation_ar":"have + المفعول + التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"","options":["My father has had his car servicing twice this year.","My father has had serviced his car twice this year.","My father has his car service twice this year.","My father has had his car serviced twice this year."],"answer":"My father has had his car serviced twice this year.","explanation":"Change the tense of have/get.","explanation_ar":"زمن have/get."},{"q":"Saad ___ his wallet stolen at the stadium.","options":["got to","did","had","made"],"answer":"had","explanation":"have + object + past participle.","explanation_ar":"have + المفعول + التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"I'm going to get my essay ___ by my English teacher.","options":["checked","check","to check","checking"],"answer":"checked","explanation":"get + object + past participle (informal).","explanation_ar":"get للتعبير غير الرسمي."},{"q":"\"I'll have my portfolio printed.\" Who will print it?","options":["Nobody will print it","My printer printed it yesterday","I will print it myself","Someone else, probably a print shop"],"answer":"Someone else, probably a print shop","explanation":"Object before the past participle.","explanation_ar":"المفعول قبل التصريف الثالث."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Faisal in a small framing shop in an old souq, handing calligraphy pieces to an elderly framer; a print shop with a big poster coming out of a printer; his brother photographing artwork; a cracked frame on a counter. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Faisal in a small framing shop in an old souq, handing calligraphy pieces to an elderly framer; a print shop with a big poster coming out of a printer; his brother photographing artwork; a cracked frame on a counter"},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about causative have / get + object + past participle (a service someone else does for us); have + person + base verb; tenses of the causative; bad experiences (had my phone stolen), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about causative have / get + object + past participle (a service someone else does for us)"},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows exhibition (a public show of art or other interesting things); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing exhibition: a public show of art or other interesting things"},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows calligraphy (the art of beautiful handwriting); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing calligraphy: the art of beautiful handwriting"},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows sculpture (a piece of art made by shaping stone, wood, metal or clay); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing sculpture: a piece of art made by shaping stone, wood, metal or clay"},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows mosaic (a picture made from many small pieces of colored stone, glass or tile); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing mosaic: a picture made from many small pieces of colored stone, glass or tile"},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Grammar Hot Seat”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Grammar Hot Seat"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS1-W01","script":"exhibition. exhibition. The school art exhibition opens on Thursday.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS1-W02","script":"calligraphy. calligraphy. Arabic calligraphy decorates many mosques.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS1-W03","script":"sculpture. sculpture. There's a huge sculpture of a falcon in the square.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS1-W04","script":"mosaic. mosaic. The mosque floor has a beautiful blue mosaic.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS1-T1","script":"Next month, our school is holding its first art exhibition, and I'm getting everything ready for my Arabic calligraphy display. I can write the calligraphy myself, but I can't do everything alone. Last week, I had my best pieces framed at a small shop in the old souq. The framer, Mr. Hasan, has worked there for forty years, and his frames are beautiful. Yesterday, I got the large poster printed at a print shop near the school because our printer is too small. My brother, Ziyad, is a photographer, so I had him take photos of each piece for the online catalog. He's very patient – he took more than two hundred photos! There's one problem: one of my frames was cracked when I picked it up. I'm having it repaired this week. I also need to get my name engraved on a small brass plate for each frame. On the day of the exhibition, I'm going to have the lights checked by the school technician, because good lighting makes calligraphy shine. I'm nervous, but I'm also excited. My grandfather, who taught me my first letters, is coming to see the show!","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “I Had My Calligraphy Framed: Causative have / get something done”. Let’s learn causative have / get + object + past participle (a service someone else does for us); have + person + base verb; tenses of the causative; bad experiences (had my phone stolen) together. Listen to the start of “Getting Ready for the Exhibition – Faisal”: Next month, our school is holding its first art exhibition, and I'm getting everything ready for my Arabic calligraphy display. I can write the calligraphy myself, but I can't do everything alone. Look at the green words. We use the causative when someone else does a job or service for us: I had my pieces framed. (Mr. Hasan framed them – I didn't.) Form: have + object + past participle. get + object + past participle means the same but is more informal: I got the poster printed. Change the tense of have / get to show the time: I'm having it repaired this week. I had it repaired last week. I'll get it repaired tomorrow. I've had it repaired twice. We can add by + person: I'm going to have the lights checked by the school technician. Here are some examples. We had our house painted before Eid. Lina gets her eyes tested every year. I'm having my thobe shortened at the tailor's. Be careful! Some learners say: “I cut my hair at the barber's. (the barber did it).” That’s not right. We say: “I had my hair cut at the barber's.” Someone else did it → causative. Quick check: \"I had my pieces framed.\" Did I frame them? … Think! … No – the framer did. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I had my calligraphy framed\" and \"I'm getting my phone repaired.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS2","title":"Our Teacher Made Us Start Again: make, let and allow","objectives":["Students will be able to describe obligation and permission with make, let and allow + object.","Students will be able to use the correct verb form after each verb, including in the passive.","I can say \"Our teacher made us start again\" and \"My parents let me paint my room.\"","I can say \"Visitors aren't allowed to take photos.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من وصف الإلزام والإذن بـ make وlet وallow + المفعول.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام صيغة الفعل الصحيحة بعد كل فعل، ومنها في المبني للمجهول.","أستطيع أن أقول Our teacher made us start again وMy parents let me paint my room.","أستطيع أن أقول Visitors aren't allowed to take photos."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"masterpiece","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmæstɚˌpis/","definition":"an artist's best and most famous work","arabic":"تحفة فنية","example":"This painting is considered a masterpiece.","image_id":"GV-L07-U6-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS2-W01"},{"word":"inspire","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈspaɪr/","definition":"to give someone the wish and ideas to create something","arabic":"يُلهِم","example":"The desert inspired many of her paintings.","image_id":"GV-L07-U6-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS2-W02"},{"word":"imagination","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪˌmædʒəˈneɪʃən/","definition":"the ability to create pictures and ideas in your mind","arabic":"خيال","example":"You need a lot of imagination to write stories.","image_id":"GV-L07-U6-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS2-W03"},{"word":"talented","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈtæləntɪd/","definition":"having a natural ability to do something well","arabic":"موهوب","example":"My cousin is a talented photographer.","image_id":"GV-L07-U6-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"make + person + base verb = force or require someone to do something: Our teacher made us start again. (We had no choice.) It can also mean \"cause\": Sad songs make me feel calm.\nlet + person + base verb = give permission: My parents let me paint my room. allow + person + to + verb means the same but is more formal: The museum doesn't allow visitors to take photos. Note: make and let have no to; allow needs to.\nIn the passive, make needs to: We were made to wait outside. allow → We are allowed to use the art room. let has no passive – use be allowed to instead: (not: We were let to go) → We were allowed to go. help can take the base verb or to: She helped me (to) finish the mural.\nmake + person + base verb (no to)\nlet + person + base verb (no to)\nallow + person + to + verb\npassive: be made to do • be allowed to do • (no passive with let)","examples":["Our art teacher made us clean the brushes after every lesson.","My grandfather let me use his old calligraphy pens.","The school allows students to display their work in the hall.","We were made to wear aprons in the pottery class.","Visitors aren't allowed to touch the sculptures.","That beautiful music makes me feel peaceful.","My mom won't let my little brother play with my paints.","Ms. Huda helped us choose our colors."],"common_errors":["✗ The teacher made us to start again. → ✓ The teacher made us start again. (make + person + base verb.)","✗ My parents let me to paint my room. → ✓ My parents let me paint my room. (let + person + base verb.)","✗ The museum doesn't allow visitors take photos. → ✓ The museum doesn't allow visitors to take photos. (allow + person + to + verb.)","✗ We were let to leave early. → ✓ We were allowed to leave early. (No passive with let.)"],"arabic":"make + الشخص + المصدر (دون to) = يُجبر: Our teacher made us start again.\nlet + الشخص + المصدر (دون to) = يسمح: My parents let me paint my room.\nallow + الشخص + to + الفعل = يسمح (أكثر رسمية).\nفي المبني للمجهول: be made to do وbe allowed to do، ولا نستخدم let في المجهول."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Our Teacher Made Us Start Again: make, let and allow”. Let’s learn make + object + base verb (force/require); let + object + base verb (permit); allow + object + to + verb; passive: be made to do, be allowed to do (no passive with let); help + object + (to) + verb together.","on_screen":"GV-L07-U6-LS2 | Our Teacher Made Us Start Again: make, let and allow","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: The coach made us run five laps. • Dad let me use his camera. The guard didn't let us enter. • We weren't allowed to touch the paintings. Will your parents let you go to the art camp? • Are we allowed to use paint here?","on_screen":"The coach made us run five laps. • Dad let me use his camera. | The guard didn't let us enter. • We weren't allowed to touch the paintings. | Will your parents let you go to the art camp? • Are we allowed to use paint here?","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"make + person + base verb = force or require someone to do something: Our teacher made us start again. (We had no choice.) It can also mean \"cause\": Sad songs make me feel calm. let + person + base verb = give permission: My parents let me paint my room. allow + person + to + verb means the same but is more formal: The museum doesn't allow visitors to take photos. Note: make and let have no to; allow needs to.","on_screen":"make + person + base verb (no to) • let + person + base verb (no to) • allow + person + to + verb","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Our art teacher made us clean the brushes after every lesson. My grandfather let me use his old calligraphy pens. The school allows students to display their work in the hall.","on_screen":"Our art teacher made us clean the brushes after every lesson. / My grandfather let me use his old calligraphy pens. / The school allows students to display their work in the hall.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The teacher made us to start again.” That’s not right. We say: “The teacher made us start again.” make + person + base verb.","on_screen":"✗ The teacher made us to start again.   ✓ The teacher made us start again.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"The teacher made us start again.\" Did we want to start again? … Think! … Probably not – we had to. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"Our teacher made us start again\" and \"My parents let me paint my room.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"Our teacher made us start again\" and \"My parents let me paint my room.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: make + object + base verb (force/require); let + object + base verb (permit); allow + object + to + verb; passive: be made to do, be allowed to do (no passive with let); help + object + (to) + verb.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","make + الشخص + المصدر (دون to) = يُجبر: Our teacher made us start again.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The teacher made us to start again. — الصحيح: The teacher made us start again.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول Our teacher made us start again وMy parents let me paint my room."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Our art teacher made us ___ the sketch again.","options":["drew","to draw","draw","drawing"],"answer":"draw","explanation":"make + person + base verb (force).","explanation_ar":"make للإجبار."},{"q":"My parents let me ___ my bedroom wall.","options":["painting","to paint","paint","painted"],"answer":"paint","explanation":"let + person + base verb (permission).","explanation_ar":"let للإذن."},{"q":"The museum doesn't allow visitors ___ photos.","options":["to take","take","taking","took"],"answer":"to take","explanation":"allow + person + to + verb.","explanation_ar":"allow مع to."},{"q":"","options":["We made to wait outside the gallery.","We were made wait outside the gallery.","We were let to wait outside the gallery.","We were made to wait outside the gallery."],"answer":"We were made to wait outside the gallery.","explanation":"be made to / be allowed to (no passive with let).","explanation_ar":"المبني للمجهول."},{"q":"","options":["Students are let to use the art room after school.","Students are allowed to use the art room after school.","Students are allowed use the art room after school.","Students allow to use the art room after school."],"answer":"Students are allowed to use the art room after school.","explanation":"be made to / be allowed to (no passive with let).","explanation_ar":"المبني للمجهول."},{"q":"Our coach helped us ___ the mural on the gym wall.","options":["to finishing","finish","finishing","finished"],"answer":"finish","explanation":"help + person + (to) + verb.","explanation_ar":"help."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS2-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with the correct form. Word bank: use, to touch, practice","items":[{"q":"The teacher didn't let us ______ (use) our phones in the gallery.","options":[],"answer":"use","explanation":"let + person + base verb (permission).","explanation_ar":"let للإذن."},{"q":"My grandfather made me ______ (practice) calligraphy every day.","options":[],"answer":"practice","explanation":"make + person + base verb (force).","explanation_ar":"make للإجبار."},{"q":"Are we allowed ______ (touch) the sculptures?","options":[],"answer":"to touch","explanation":"allow + person + to + verb.","explanation_ar":"allow مع to."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Rewrite with the verb in brackets.","items":[{"q":"The teacher said to us, \"You must start again.\" (make)","options":[],"answer":"The teacher made us start again.","explanation":"make + person + base verb (force).","explanation_ar":"make للإجبار."},{"q":"Dad said, \"OK, you can go to the art fair.\" (let)","options":[],"answer":"Dad let me go to the art fair.","explanation":"let + person + base verb (permission).","explanation_ar":"let للإذن."},{"q":"The rules say visitors can't use flash. (allow)","options":[],"answer":"The rules don't allow visitors to use flash.","explanation":"allow + person + to + verb.","explanation_ar":"allow مع to."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Rules in your life.","items":[{"q":"Something your parents make you do: ___","options":[],"answer":"My parents make me finish my homework before dinner.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses make + object + base verb (force/require); let + object + base verb (permit); allow + object + to + verb; passive: be made to do, be allowed to do (no passive with let); help + object + (to) + verb correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something your parents let you do on weekends: ___","options":[],"answer":"My parents let me stay up until eleven on Thursdays.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses make + object + base verb (force/require); let + object + base verb (permit); allow + object + to + verb; passive: be made to do, be allowed to do (no passive with let); help + object + (to) + verb correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something students aren't allowed to do at school: ___","options":[],"answer":"Students aren't allowed to bring phones to class.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses make + object + base verb (force/require); let + object + base verb (permit); allow + object + to + verb; passive: be made to do, be allowed to do (no passive with let); help + object + (to) + verb correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something you were made to do when you were younger: ___","options":[],"answer":"I was made to eat vegetables every day.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses make + object + base verb (force/require); let + object + base verb (permit); allow + object + to + verb; passive: be made to do, be allowed to do (no passive with let); help + object + (to) + verb correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something that makes you feel happy: ___","options":[],"answer":"Drawing makes me feel relaxed and happy.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses make + object + base verb (force/require); let + object + base verb (permit); allow + object + to + verb; passive: be made to do, be allowed to do (no passive with let); help + object + (to) + verb correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Gallery rules.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 rules for a school art gallery with allowed / not allowed.","options":[],"answer":"Visitors aren't allowed to touch the paintings. Visitors are allowed to take photos without flash. Children aren't allowed to run.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses make + object + base verb (force/require); let + object + base verb (permit); allow + object + to + verb; passive: be made to do, be allowed to do (no passive with let); help + object + (to) + verb correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about what a good art teacher makes or lets students do.","options":[],"answer":"A good art teacher lets students choose their own topics. She makes them plan before they paint.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses make + object + base verb (force/require); let + object + base verb (permit); allow + object + to + verb; passive: be made to do, be allowed to do (no passive with let); help + object + (to) + verb correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with help + person + verb.","options":[],"answer":"My cousin helped me design my poster.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses make + object + base verb (force/require); let + object + base verb (permit); allow + object + to + verb; passive: be made to do, be allowed to do (no passive with let); help + object + (to) + verb correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Sentence Builder Race","mechanic":"sentence_builder","rules":["Each team receives the same tile set.","In 5 minutes, build as many different correct sentences as possible using make + object + base verb (force/require); let + object + base verb (permit); allow + object + to + verb; passive: be made to do, be allowed to do (no passive with let); help + object + (to) + verb.","Write each sentence on the team sheet.","Swap sheets with another team to check. One point per correct sentence; no points for repeats."],"data":[{"cue":"my calligraphy / frame (had)"},{"cue":"the poster / print (got)"},{"cue":"my phone screen / repair (am having)"},{"cue":"my hair / cut (will get)"},{"cue":"the teacher / make us / redo the sketch"},{"cue":"my parents / let me / paint my room"},{"cue":"the museum / not allow / visitors / take photos"},{"cue":"we / be made / wait outside"},{"cue":"the coach / let us / leave early"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The guard didn't let us ___ the museum after 6 p.m.","options":["to enter","entering","enter","entered"],"answer":"enter","explanation":"let + person + base verb (permission).","explanation_ar":"let للإذن."},{"q":"My mother makes me ___ my room every Saturday.","options":["tidy","tidying","tidied","to tidy"],"answer":"tidy","explanation":"make + person + base verb (force).","explanation_ar":"make للإجبار."},{"q":"The new rules allow students ___ their own art supplies.","options":["bringing","to bring","brought","bring"],"answer":"to bring","explanation":"allow + person + to + verb.","explanation_ar":"allow مع to."},{"q":"","options":["We weren't let to eat in the gallery.","We weren't allowed eat in the gallery.","We didn't allow to eat in the gallery.","We weren't allowed to eat in the gallery."],"answer":"We weren't allowed to eat in the gallery.","explanation":"be made to / be allowed to (no passive with let).","explanation_ar":"المبني للمجهول."},{"q":"","options":["He was made repeat the whole project.","He made to repeat the whole project.","He was made to repeat the whole project.","He was making to repeat the whole project."],"answer":"He was made to repeat the whole project.","explanation":"be made to / be allowed to (no passive with let).","explanation_ar":"المبني للمجهول."},{"q":"Will your parents ___ you join the art camp?","options":["allow","let","let to","make to"],"answer":"let","explanation":"let + person + base verb (permission).","explanation_ar":"let للإذن."},{"q":"Funny films always ___ me laugh.","options":["allow","make","have to","let"],"answer":"make","explanation":"make + person + base verb (force).","explanation_ar":"make للإجبار."},{"q":"Ms. Huda helped me ___ the right colors for my landscape.","options":["choose","to choosing","choosing","chose"],"answer":"choose","explanation":"help + person + (to) + verb.","explanation_ar":"help."},{"q":"","options":["The school doesn't make students to leave early.","The school doesn't let students to leave early.","The school doesn't allow students leave early.","The school doesn't allow students to leave early."],"answer":"The school doesn't allow students to leave early.","explanation":"allow + person + to + verb.","explanation_ar":"allow مع to."},{"q":"\"The teacher let me redo the test.\" What does this mean?","options":["The teacher did the test.","The teacher forced me.","The teacher refused.","The teacher gave permission."],"answer":"The teacher gave permission.","explanation":"let + person + base verb (permission).","explanation_ar":"let للإذن."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"An art classroom: Ms. Huda pointing at a sketch and the student rubbing it out to start again; a sign in a gallery \"Visitors are not allowed to touch the sculptures\"; a boy happily painting his bedroom wall with his father's permission. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"An art classroom: Ms. Huda pointing at a sketch and the student rubbing it out to start again; a sign in a gallery \"Visitors are not allowed to touch the sculptures\"; a boy happily painting his bedroom wall with his father's permission"},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of make + object + base verb (force/require); let + object + base verb (permit); allow + object + to + verb; passive: be made to do, be allowed to do (no passive with let); help + object + (to) + verb: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Arts and Creativity”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of make + object + base verb (force/require)"},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows masterpiece (an artist's best and most famous work); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing masterpiece: an artist's best and most famous work"},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows inspire (to give someone the wish and ideas to create something); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing inspire: to give someone the wish and ideas to create something"},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows imagination (the ability to create pictures and ideas in your mind); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing imagination: the ability to create pictures and ideas in your mind"},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows talented (having a natural ability to do something well); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing talented: having a natural ability to do something well"},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Sentence Builder Race”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Sentence Builder Race"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS2-W01","script":"masterpiece. masterpiece. This painting is considered a masterpiece.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS2-W02","script":"inspire. inspire. The desert inspired many of her paintings.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS2-W03","script":"imagination. imagination. You need a lot of imagination to write stories.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS2-W04","script":"talented. talented. My cousin is a talented photographer.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Our Teacher Made Us Start Again: make, let and allow”. Let’s learn make + object + base verb (force/require); let + object + base verb (permit); allow + object + to + verb; passive: be made to do, be allowed to do (no passive with let); help + object + (to) + verb together. Remember these patterns: The coach made us run five laps. • Dad let me use his camera. The guard didn't let us enter. • We weren't allowed to touch the paintings. Will your parents let you go to the art camp? • Are we allowed to use paint here? make + person + base verb = force or require someone to do something: Our teacher made us start again. (We had no choice.) It can also mean \"cause\": Sad songs make me feel calm. let + person + base verb = give permission: My parents let me paint my room. allow + person + to + verb means the same but is more formal: The museum doesn't allow visitors to take photos. Note: make and let have no to; allow needs to. Here are some examples. Our art teacher made us clean the brushes after every lesson. My grandfather let me use his old calligraphy pens. The school allows students to display their work in the hall. Be careful! Some learners say: “The teacher made us to start again.” That’s not right. We say: “The teacher made us start again.” make + person + base verb. Quick check: \"The teacher made us start again.\" Did we want to start again? … Think! … Probably not – we had to. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"Our teacher made us start again\" and \"My parents let me paint my room.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS3","title":"Creative, Colorful, Priceless: Art Words and Adjective Suffixes","objectives":["Students will be able to describe art with precise vocabulary.","Students will be able to form and use adjectives with -ful, -less, -ous and -ive.","I can describe a work of art with words like abstract, expressive and decorative.","I can make adjectives like colorful, careless, mysterious and creative."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من وصف الفن بمفردات دقيقة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من تكوين الصفات باللواحق -ful و-less و-ous و-ive واستخدامها.","أستطيع أن أصف عملًا فنيًّا بكلمات مثل abstract وexpressive وdecorative.","أستطيع أن أكوّن صفات مثل colorful وcareless وmysterious وcreative."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"abstract","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/æbˈstrækt/","definition":"using shapes and colors instead of showing real things","arabic":"تجريدي","example":"I don't always understand abstract art.","image_id":"GV-L07-U6-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS3-W01"},{"word":"landscape","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈlændˌskeɪp/","definition":"a painting or photo of an area of land, such as mountains or valleys","arabic":"منظر طبيعي","example":"He painted a landscape of the Asir mountains.","image_id":"GV-L07-U6-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS3-W02"},{"word":"gallery","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɡælɚi/","definition":"a building or room where art is shown","arabic":"صالة عرض / معرض فني","example":"We visited a small gallery in Jeddah.","image_id":"GV-L07-U6-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS3-W03"},{"word":"sketch","pos":"noun","ipa":"/skɛtʃ/","definition":"a quick, simple drawing","arabic":"رسم تخطيطي","example":"She made a sketch before she started painting.","image_id":"GV-L07-U6-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS3-W04"},{"word":"expressive","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ɪkˈsprɛsɪv/","definition":"showing feelings and meaning clearly","arabic":"معبِّر","example":"Her calligraphy is very expressive.","image_id":"GV-L07-U6-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS3-W05"},{"word":"decorative","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈdɛkrətɪv/","definition":"beautiful and used to make something look nice","arabic":"زخرفي / تزييني","example":"The box has decorative patterns on the lid.","image_id":"GV-L07-U6-LS3-W06","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS3-W06"}],"explanation":{"text":"Art words: exhibition, gallery, calligraphy, sculpture, mosaic, sketch, landscape, masterpiece, abstract, expressive, decorative, talented, imagination, inspire.\nSuffixes make adjectives: -ful = full of (colorful, peaceful, skillful, meaningful); -less = without (colorless, careless, pointless, endless); -ous = having the quality of (famous, mysterious, glorious, nervous); -ive = tending to (creative, expressive, decorative, imaginative, impressive).\nBe careful: priceless means extremely valuable (too valuable to have a price), not \"worth nothing\" – that's worthless. Spelling changes: beauty → beautiful; mystery → mysterious; create → creative; imagine → imaginative.\nWord families: create: creative (adj), creation (n), creativity (n) | imagine: imaginative (adj), imagination (n) | express: expressive (adj), expression (n) | decorate: decorative (adj), decoration (n) | color: colorful (adj), colorless (adj) | mystery: mysterious (adj), mysteriously (adv) | impress: impressive (adj), impression (n)","examples":["Her colorful mosaics brighten the whole hall.","The abstract painting is full of circles and lines.","His calligraphy is expressive and skillful.","The museum's oldest manuscript is priceless.","The desert inspired many imaginative stories.","That was a careless mistake – check your spelling.","The sculpture has a mysterious smile.","The new mural is truly impressive."],"common_errors":["✗ The painting is very color. → ✓ The painting is very colorful. (Adjective → colorful.)","✗ She is a very creation artist. → ✓ She is a very creative artist. (Adjective → creative.)","✗ The old map is priceless, so it's worth nothing. → ✓ The old map is priceless, so it's worth a fortune. (priceless = extremely valuable.)","✗ It was a mystery story with a mysterious ending. (spelling: mysterous) → ✓ mysterious (Spelling: mysterious.)"],"arabic":"كلمات الفن: exhibition (معرض) وcalligraphy (الخط) وsculpture (منحوتة) وmosaic (فسيفساء) وmasterpiece (تحفة فنية).\nاللواحق: -ful (مليء بـ) colorful، و-less (بدون) careless، و-ous (ذو صفة) famous، و-ive creative.\nانتبه: priceless تعني «لا يُقدَّر بثمن» أي غالٍ جدًّا، وليس «بلا قيمة» (worthless).\nتتغير التهجئة أحيانًا: beauty → beautiful، mystery → mysterious."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Creative, Colorful, Priceless: Art Words and Adjective Suffixes”. Let’s learn art vocabulary; adjective suffixes -ful, -less, -ous, -ive (colorful, colorless, mysterious, creative); word families (create → creative → creation → creativity) together.","on_screen":"GV-L07-U6-LS3 | Creative, Colorful, Priceless: Art Words and Adjective Suffixes","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. abstract: using shapes and colors instead of showing real things. landscape: a painting or photo of an area of land, such as mountains or valleys. gallery: a building or room where art is shown.","on_screen":"abstract | landscape | gallery","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Art words: exhibition, gallery, calligraphy, sculpture, mosaic, sketch, landscape, masterpiece, abstract, expressive, decorative, talented, imagination, inspire. Suffixes make adjectives: -ful = full of (colorful, peaceful, skillful, meaningful); -less = without (colorless, careless, pointless, endless); -ous = having the quality of (famous, mysterious, glorious, nervous); -ive = tending to (creative, expressive, decorative, imaginative, impressive).","on_screen":"art vocabulary; adjective suffixes -ful, -less, -ous, -ive (colorful, colorless, mysterious, creative); word families (create → creative → creation → creativity)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Her colorful mosaics brighten the whole hall. The abstract painting is full of circles and lines. His calligraphy is expressive and skillful.","on_screen":"Her colorful mosaics brighten the whole hall. / The abstract painting is full of circles and lines. / His calligraphy is expressive and skillful.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The painting is very color.” That’s not right. We say: “The painting is very colorful.” Adjective → colorful.","on_screen":"✗ The painting is very color.   ✓ The painting is very colorful.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Is a \"priceless\" painting cheap or extremely valuable? … Think! … Extremely valuable. Great job! Now you can say: I can describe a work of art with words like abstract, expressive and decorative.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can describe a work of art with words like abstract, expressive and decorative.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: art vocabulary; adjective suffixes -ful, -less, -ous, -ive (colorful, colorless, mysterious, creative); word families (create → creative → creation → creativity).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","كلمات الفن: exhibition (معرض) وcalligraphy (الخط) وsculpture (منحوتة) وmosaic (فسيفساء) وmasterpiece (تحفة فنية).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The painting is very color. — الصحيح: The painting is very colorful.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أصف عملًا فنيًّا بكلمات مثل abstract وexpressive وdecorative."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"The artist made a beautiful ___ from thousands of tiny colored tiles.","options":["mosaic","sketch","gallery","landscape"],"answer":"mosaic","explanation":"Choose the art word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Her paintings are full of bright colors. They're very ___.","options":["colorly","colorful","colored in","colorless"],"answer":"colorful","explanation":"Choose the right suffix (-ful, -less, -ous, -ive).","explanation_ar":"اللاحقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"The ending of the story was strange and hard to explain. It was ___.","options":["mysteried","mysteriously","mysterious","mystery"],"answer":"mysterious","explanation":"Choose the right suffix (-ful, -less, -ous, -ive).","explanation_ar":"اللاحقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"A painting of mountains, valleys and rivers is a ___.","options":["landscape","calligraphy","sculpture","mosaic"],"answer":"landscape","explanation":"Choose the art word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Children have amazing ___; they can invent whole worlds.","options":["imaginary","imagine","imaginative","imagination"],"answer":"imagination","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form.","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة."},{"q":"The old necklace is ___ – it's worth a huge amount of money.","options":["pointless","priceless","worthless","careless"],"answer":"priceless","explanation":"Tricky meanings (priceless vs worthless).","explanation_ar":"المعنى الدقيق."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the word to its meaning.","items":[{"q":"gallery","options":["a piece of art made from stone, wood or metal","to give someone the wish and ideas to create something","a quick, simple drawing","an artist's best and most famous work","using shapes and colors instead of real objects","a building or room where art is shown"],"answer":"a building or room where art is shown","explanation":"gallery → a building or room where art is shown. Choose the art word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"sketch","options":["a piece of art made from stone, wood or metal","to give someone the wish and ideas to create something","a quick, simple drawing","an artist's best and most famous work","using shapes and colors instead of real objects","a building or room where art is shown"],"answer":"a quick, simple drawing","explanation":"sketch → a quick, simple drawing. Choose the art word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"sculpture","options":["a piece of art made from stone, wood or metal","to give someone the wish and ideas to create something","a quick, simple drawing","an artist's best and most famous work","using shapes and colors instead of real objects","a building or room where art is shown"],"answer":"a piece of art made from stone, wood or metal","explanation":"sculpture → a piece of art made from stone, wood or metal. Choose the art word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"abstract","options":["a piece of art made from stone, wood or metal","to give someone the wish and ideas to create something","a quick, simple drawing","an artist's best and most famous work","using shapes and colors instead of real objects","a building or room where art is shown"],"answer":"using shapes and colors instead of real objects","explanation":"abstract → using shapes and colors instead of real objects. Choose the art word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"masterpiece","options":["a piece of art made from stone, wood or metal","to give someone the wish and ideas to create something","a quick, simple drawing","an artist's best and most famous work","using shapes and colors instead of real objects","a building or room where art is shown"],"answer":"an artist's best and most famous work","explanation":"masterpiece → an artist's best and most famous work. Choose the art word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"inspire","options":["a piece of art made from stone, wood or metal","to give someone the wish and ideas to create something","a quick, simple drawing","an artist's best and most famous work","using shapes and colors instead of real objects","a building or room where art is shown"],"answer":"to give someone the wish and ideas to create something","explanation":"inspire → to give someone the wish and ideas to create something. Choose the art word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Talk about art.","items":[{"q":"Describe your favorite piece of art with two adjectives.","options":[],"answer":"My favorite piece is a calligraphy panel; it's elegant and expressive.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses art vocabulary; adjective suffixes -ful, -less, -ous, -ive (colorful, colorless, mysterious, creative); word families (create → creative → creation → creativity) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something that inspires you: ___","options":[],"answer":"The mountains of Taif inspire me to draw.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses art vocabulary; adjective suffixes -ful, -less, -ous, -ive (colorful, colorless, mysterious, creative); word families (create → creative → creation → creativity) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with a -less adjective.","options":[],"answer":"The desert at night seems endless.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses art vocabulary; adjective suffixes -ful, -less, -ous, -ive (colorful, colorless, mysterious, creative); word families (create → creative → creation → creativity) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with an -ous adjective.","options":[],"answer":"The artist is famous for his mosaics.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses art vocabulary; adjective suffixes -ful, -less, -ous, -ive (colorful, colorless, mysterious, creative); word families (create → creative → creation → creativity) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"creativity\".","options":[],"answer":"Our school encourages creativity in every subject.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses art vocabulary; adjective suffixes -ful, -less, -ous, -ive (colorful, colorless, mysterious, creative); word families (create → creative → creation → creativity) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Art review.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 sentences describing a painting, sculpture or mosaic you know.","options":[],"answer":"The mosaic in the mosque is blue and gold. It has decorative patterns. It looks peaceful and impressive.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses art vocabulary; adjective suffixes -ful, -less, -ous, -ive (colorful, colorless, mysterious, creative); word families (create → creative → creation → creativity) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences with \"talented\" and \"imaginative\".","options":[],"answer":"My cousin is a talented sculptor. His animals are imaginative and full of life.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses art vocabulary; adjective suffixes -ful, -less, -ous, -ive (colorful, colorless, mysterious, creative); word families (create → creative → creation → creativity) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence about why art is important.","options":[],"answer":"Art is important because it helps us express feelings that words can't explain.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses art vocabulary; adjective suffixes -ful, -less, -ous, -ive (colorful, colorless, mysterious, creative); word families (create → creative → creation → creativity) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Family Tree","mechanic":"drag_and_drop","rules":["Teams take turns drawing a word card.","Place the card on the correct branch of the tree and say a sentence with it.","Correct placement and sentence = 2 points.","The team with the most points when the tree is full wins."],"data":[{"word":"creative","category":"adjective","family":"create"},{"word":"creation","category":"noun","family":"create"},{"word":"creativity","category":"noun","family":"create"},{"word":"imaginative","category":"adjective","family":"imagine"},{"word":"imagination","category":"noun","family":"imagine"},{"word":"expressive","category":"adjective","family":"express"},{"word":"expression","category":"noun","family":"express"},{"word":"decorative","category":"adjective","family":"decorate"},{"word":"decoration","category":"noun","family":"decorate"},{"word":"colorful","category":"adjective","family":"color"},{"word":"colorless","category":"adjective","family":"color"},{"word":"mysterious","category":"adjective","family":"mystery"},{"word":"mysteriously","category":"adverb","family":"mystery"},{"word":"impressive","category":"adjective","family":"impress"},{"word":"impression","category":"noun","family":"impress"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The ___ of the new library won a design prize.","options":["decoratively","decorative","decoration","decorate"],"answer":"decoration","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form.","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة."},{"q":"Ziyad is a ___ photographer; his photos win prizes every year.","options":["talentless","talented","talentful","talent"],"answer":"talented","explanation":"Choose the art word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Don't be ___! Check your work before you hand it in.","options":["cared","careless","caring","careful"],"answer":"careless","explanation":"Choose the right suffix (-ful, -less, -ous, -ive).","explanation_ar":"اللاحقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"The visitors were amazed. The exhibition was very ___.","options":["impress","impression","impressive","impressed by"],"answer":"impressive","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form.","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة."},{"q":"This vase is ___ – it's only plastic, and it's broken.","options":["valuable","precious","priceless","worthless"],"answer":"worthless","explanation":"Tricky meanings (priceless vs worthless).","explanation_ar":"المعنى الدقيق."},{"q":"Her drawings show strong feelings. They're very ___.","options":["expressive","express","expressively","expression"],"answer":"expressive","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form.","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة."},{"q":"He made a quick ___ of the mosque before painting it.","options":["gallery","sculpture","sketch","masterpiece"],"answer":"sketch","explanation":"Choose the art word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"The sunset over the Red Sea was ___.","options":["gloriously","glorious","glory","gloryful"],"answer":"glorious","explanation":"Choose the right suffix (-ful, -less, -ous, -ive).","explanation_ar":"اللاحقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"The garden was quiet and calm – very ___.","options":["peaceful","peacive","peaceous","peaceless"],"answer":"peaceful","explanation":"Choose the right suffix (-ful, -less, -ous, -ive).","explanation_ar":"اللاحقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"Art lessons help students develop their ___.","options":["create","creative","creatively","creativity"],"answer":"creativity","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form.","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A gallery wall with four works: a colorful abstract painting, a landscape of the Asir mountains, a blue tile mosaic and a decorative calligraphy panel; small labels show adjectives ending in -ful, -less, -ous and -ive. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A gallery wall with four works: a colorful abstract painting, a landscape of the Asir mountains, a blue tile mosaic and a decorative calligraphy panel; small labels show adjectives ending in -ful, -less, -ous and -ive"},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 6 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 6 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows abstract (using shapes and colors instead of showing real things); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing abstract: using shapes and colors instead of showing real things"},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows landscape (a painting or photo of an area of land, such as mountains or valleys); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing landscape: a painting or photo of an area of land, such as mountains or valleys"},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows gallery (a building or room where art is shown); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing gallery: a building or room where art is shown"},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows sketch (a quick, simple drawing); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing sketch: a quick, simple drawing"},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows expressive (showing feelings and meaning clearly); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing expressive: showing feelings and meaning clearly"},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS3-W06","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows decorative (beautiful and used to make something look nice); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing decorative: beautiful and used to make something look nice"},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Family Tree”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Family Tree"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS3-W01","script":"abstract. abstract. I don't always understand abstract art.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS3-W02","script":"landscape. landscape. He painted a landscape of the Asir mountains.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS3-W03","script":"gallery. gallery. We visited a small gallery in Jeddah.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS3-W04","script":"sketch. sketch. She made a sketch before she started painting.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS3-W05","script":"expressive. expressive. Her calligraphy is very expressive.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS3-W06","script":"decorative. decorative. The box has decorative patterns on the lid.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Creative, Colorful, Priceless: Art Words and Adjective Suffixes”. Let’s learn art vocabulary; adjective suffixes -ful, -less, -ous, -ive (colorful, colorless, mysterious, creative); word families (create → creative → creation → creativity) together. Meet some new words. abstract: using shapes and colors instead of showing real things. landscape: a painting or photo of an area of land, such as mountains or valleys. gallery: a building or room where art is shown. Art words: exhibition, gallery, calligraphy, sculpture, mosaic, sketch, landscape, masterpiece, abstract, expressive, decorative, talented, imagination, inspire. Suffixes make adjectives: -ful = full of (colorful, peaceful, skillful, meaningful); -less = without (colorless, careless, pointless, endless); -ous = having the quality of (famous, mysterious, glorious, nervous); -ive = tending to (creative, expressive, decorative, imaginative, impressive). Here are some examples. Her colorful mosaics brighten the whole hall. The abstract painting is full of circles and lines. His calligraphy is expressive and skillful. Be careful! Some learners say: “The painting is very color.” That’s not right. We say: “The painting is very colorful.” Adjective → colorful. Quick check: Is a \"priceless\" painting cheap or extremely valuable? … Think! … Extremely valuable. Great job! Now you can say: I can describe a work of art with words like abstract, expressive and decorative.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS4","title":"A Bright, Colorful Mosaic: Commas with Coordinate Adjectives","objectives":["Students will be able to tell coordinate adjectives from cumulative adjectives.","Students will be able to put commas between coordinate adjectives and nowhere else.","I can write \"a bright, colorful mosaic\" with a comma.","I can write \"a small wooden box\" without a comma."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من التمييز بين الصفات المتساوية والصفات المتراكمة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من وضع الفواصل بين الصفات المتساوية فقط.","أستطيع أن أكتب a bright, colorful mosaic بفاصلة.","أستطيع أن أكتب a small wooden box دون فاصلة."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"exhibition","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɛksəˈbɪʃən/","definition":"a public show of art or other interesting things","arabic":"معرض","example":"The school art exhibition opens on Thursday.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"calligraphy","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kəˈlɪɡrəfi/","definition":"the art of beautiful handwriting","arabic":"فن الخط","example":"Arabic calligraphy decorates many mosques.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"sculpture","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈskʌlptʃɚ/","definition":"a piece of art made by shaping stone, wood, metal or clay","arabic":"منحوتة / مجسّم","example":"There's a huge sculpture of a falcon in the square.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"mosaic","pos":"noun","ipa":"/moʊˈzeɪɪk/","definition":"a picture made from many small pieces of colored stone, glass or tile","arabic":"فسيفساء","example":"The mosque floor has a beautiful blue mosaic.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"masterpiece","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmæstɚˌpis/","definition":"an artist's best and most famous work","arabic":"تحفة فنية","example":"This painting is considered a masterpiece.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"inspire","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈspaɪr/","definition":"to give someone the wish and ideas to create something","arabic":"يُلهِم","example":"The desert inspired many of her paintings.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Coordinate adjectives describe a noun equally. Put a comma between them: a bright, colorful mosaic; a long, boring speech. Two tests: (1) Can you switch the order? (a colorful, bright mosaic ✓) (2) Can you put and between them? (a bright and colorful mosaic ✓) If yes, use a comma.\nCumulative adjectives build on each other in a fixed order (opinion – size – age – shape – color – origin – material – purpose + noun). Don't use a comma: a small wooden box; a beautiful old Persian carpet. The tests fail: (not: a wooden small box), (not: a small and wooden box) (sounds wrong).\nNever put a comma between the last adjective and the noun: (not: a bright, colorful, mosaic). Numbers and words like two, many, several don't take commas either: three old books.\nswitch the order + add \"and\" sounds fine → comma\nfixed order (opinion-size-age-shape-color-origin-material) → no comma\nno comma before the noun\nno comma after numbers (two, three, several)","examples":["It was a bright, colorful mosaic.","She bought a small wooden box.","The gallery had cool, quiet rooms.","He wore a new black jacket.","We walked through a long, narrow, dark corridor.","My grandmother has a beautiful old Persian carpet.","The poet gave a thoughtful, moving speech.","There were two huge bronze sculptures at the entrance."],"common_errors":["✗ It was a bright colorful mosaic. → ✓ It was a bright, colorful mosaic. (Coordinate → comma.)","✗ She has a lovely, silver necklace. → ✓ She has a lovely silver necklace. (Cumulative (opinion + material) → no comma.)","✗ It was a calm, peaceful, landscape. → ✓ It was a calm, peaceful landscape. (No comma before the noun.)","✗ an old beautiful Persian carpet → ✓ a beautiful old Persian carpet (Opinion comes before age.)"],"arabic":"الصفات المتساوية (coordinate) تصف الاسم بالدرجة نفسها، فنضع بينها فاصلة: a bright, colorful mosaic.\nاختبار: هل يمكن تبديل ترتيبها ووضع and بينها؟ إذا نعم ← فاصلة.\nالصفات المتراكمة (cumulative) لها ترتيب ثابت (رأي – حجم – عمر – شكل – لون – أصل – مادة) فلا فاصلة: a small wooden box.\nلا نضع فاصلة بين آخر صفة والاسم، ولا بعد الأعداد."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Bright, Colorful Mosaic: Commas with Coordinate Adjectives”. Let’s learn coordinate adjectives (equal, can switch order and add \"and\" → comma) vs cumulative adjectives (in fixed order → no comma); no comma between the last adjective and the noun; adjective order together.","on_screen":"GV-L07-U6-LS4 | A Bright, Colorful Mosaic: Commas with Coordinate Adjectives","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Coordinate adjectives describe a noun equally. Put a comma between them: a bright, colorful mosaic; a long, boring speech. Two tests: (1) Can you switch the order? (a colorful, bright mosaic ✓) (2) Can you put and between them? (a bright and colorful mosaic ✓) If yes, use a comma.","on_screen":"coordinate adjectives (equal, can switch order and add \"and\" → comma) vs cumulative adjectives (in fixed order → no comma); no comma between the last adjective and the noun; adjective order","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Coordinate adjectives describe a noun equally. Put a comma between them: a bright, colorful mosaic; a long, boring speech. Two tests: (1) Can you switch the order? (a colorful, bright mosaic ✓) (2) Can you put and between them? (a bright and colorful mosaic ✓) If yes, use a comma. Cumulative adjectives build on each other in a fixed order (opinion – size – age – shape – color – origin – material – purpose + noun). Don't use a comma: a small wooden box; a beautiful old Persian carpet. The tests fail: (not: a wooden small box), (not: a small and wooden box) (sounds wrong).","on_screen":"switch the order + add \"and\" sounds fine → comma • fixed order (opinion-size-age-shape-color-origin-material) → no comma • no comma before the noun","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. It was a bright, colorful mosaic. She bought a small wooden box. The gallery had cool, quiet rooms.","on_screen":"It was a bright, colorful mosaic. / She bought a small wooden box. / The gallery had cool, quiet rooms.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “It was a bright colorful mosaic.” That’s not right. We say: “It was a bright, colorful mosaic.” Coordinate → comma.","on_screen":"✗ It was a bright colorful mosaic.   ✓ It was a bright, colorful mosaic.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Can we say \"a colorful and bright mosaic\"? … Think! … Yes – so \"bright, colorful\" needs a comma. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"a bright, colorful mosaic\" with a comma.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"a bright, colorful mosaic\" with a comma.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: coordinate adjectives (equal, can switch order and add \"and\" → comma) vs cumulative adjectives (in fixed order → no comma); no comma between the last adjective and the noun; adjective order.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الصفات المتساوية (coordinate) تصف الاسم بالدرجة نفسها، فنضع بينها فاصلة: a bright, colorful mosaic.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: It was a bright colorful mosaic. — الصحيح: It was a bright, colorful mosaic.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب a bright, colorful mosaic بفاصلة."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"At the Art Gallery (editing passage)","body":"The gallery was a large bright building near the park. In the first room, there was a huge, bronze sculpture of a falcon. Next to it hung a calm, peaceful, landscape of the Asir mountains. My favorite piece was a colorful detailed mosaic made by a local artist. I bought two small, blue notebooks at the gift shop.","word_count":58,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correctly punctuated phrase.","items":[{"q":"","options":["It was a bright colorful, mosaic.","It was a, bright colorful mosaic.","It was a bright, colorful, mosaic.","It was a bright, colorful mosaic."],"answer":"It was a bright, colorful mosaic.","explanation":"Coordinate adjectives → comma.","explanation_ar":"الصفات المتساوية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["She bought a small, wooden box.","She bought a small wooden box.","She bought, a small wooden box.","She bought a small wooden, box."],"answer":"She bought a small wooden box.","explanation":"Cumulative adjectives → no comma.","explanation_ar":"الصفات المتراكمة ← بلا فاصلة."},{"q":"In which phrase do the adjectives need a comma between them?","options":["an old Arabic manuscript","a big red bus","three old books","a calm peaceful garden"],"answer":"a calm peaceful garden","explanation":"Use the \"switch\" and \"and\" tests.","explanation_ar":"اختبار التبديل وand."},{"q":"How can you check if two adjectives are coordinate?","options":["See if they both end in -ful.","Check if they are both colors.","Put \"and\" between them and switch their order.","Count the letters in each adjective."],"answer":"Put \"and\" between them and switch their order.","explanation":"Use the \"switch\" and \"and\" tests.","explanation_ar":"اختبار التبديل وand."},{"q":"","options":["The gallery had cool, quiet rooms.","The gallery had cool quiet, rooms.","The gallery had cool, quiet, rooms.","The gallery had, cool quiet rooms."],"answer":"The gallery had cool, quiet rooms.","explanation":"No comma between the last adjective and the noun.","explanation_ar":"لا فاصلة قبل الاسم."},{"q":"Which phrase has the adjectives in the correct order?","options":["a Persian beautiful old carpet","a beautiful old Persian carpet","an old beautiful Persian carpet","an old Persian beautiful carpet"],"answer":"a beautiful old Persian carpet","explanation":"Adjective order (opinion – size – age – color – origin – material).","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الصفات."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Add commas only where they are needed.","items":[{"q":"The poet gave a long boring speech.  (comma)","options":[],"answer":"The poet gave a long, boring speech.","explanation":"Coordinate adjectives → comma.","explanation_ar":"الصفات المتساوية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"He wore a new black jacket.  (no comma)","options":[],"answer":"He wore a new black jacket. (no comma)","explanation":"Cumulative adjectives → no comma.","explanation_ar":"الصفات المتراكمة ← بلا فاصلة."},{"q":"It was a cold dark windy night.  (commas)","options":[],"answer":"It was a cold, dark, windy night.","explanation":"Coordinate adjectives → comma.","explanation_ar":"الصفات المتساوية ← فاصلة."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS4-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"She has a lovely, silver necklace.","options":[],"answer":"She has a lovely silver necklace.","explanation":"lovely, silver → lovely silver. Cumulative adjectives → no comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: lovely, silver → lovely silver. الصفات المتراكمة ← بلا فاصلة."},{"q":"The loud noisy crowd cheered for the winner.","options":[],"answer":"The loud, noisy crowd cheered for the winner.","explanation":"loud noisy → loud, noisy. Coordinate adjectives → comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: loud noisy → loud, noisy. الصفات المتساوية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"It was a peaceful, beautiful, garden.","options":[],"answer":"It was a peaceful, beautiful garden.","explanation":"beautiful, garden → beautiful garden. No comma between the last adjective and the noun.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: beautiful, garden → beautiful garden. لا فاصلة قبل الاسم."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the gallery description.","items":[{"q":"The gallery was a large bright building near the park.","options":[],"answer":"The gallery was a large, bright building near the park.","explanation":"large bright → large, bright. Coordinate adjectives → comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: large bright → large, bright. الصفات المتساوية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"In the first room, there was a huge, bronze sculpture of a falcon.","options":[],"answer":"In the first room, there was a huge bronze sculpture of a falcon.","explanation":"huge, bronze → huge bronze. Coordinate adjectives → comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: huge, bronze → huge bronze. الصفات المتساوية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"Next to it hung a calm, peaceful, landscape of the Asir mountains.","options":[],"answer":"Next to it hung a calm, peaceful landscape of the Asir mountains.","explanation":"calm, peaceful, → calm, peaceful. Coordinate adjectives → comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: calm, peaceful, → calm, peaceful. الصفات المتساوية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"My favorite piece was a colorful detailed mosaic made by a local artist.","options":[],"answer":"My favorite piece was a colorful, detailed mosaic made by a local artist.","explanation":"colorful detailed → colorful, detailed. Coordinate adjectives → comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: colorful detailed → colorful, detailed. الصفات المتساوية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"I bought two small, blue notebooks at the gift shop.","options":[],"answer":"I bought two small blue notebooks at the gift shop.","explanation":"small, blue → small blue. Coordinate adjectives → comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: small, blue → small blue. الصفات المتساوية ← فاصلة."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Describe with adjectives.","items":[{"q":"Describe a place with two coordinate adjectives.","options":[],"answer":"The old souq is a busy, noisy place.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses coordinate adjectives (equal, can switch order and add \"and\" → comma) vs cumulative adjectives (in fixed order → no comma); no comma between the last adjective and the noun; adjective order correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Describe an object with two cumulative adjectives.","options":[],"answer":"I have a small silver watch.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses coordinate adjectives (equal, can switch order and add \"and\" → comma) vs cumulative adjectives (in fixed order → no comma); no comma between the last adjective and the noun; adjective order correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with three coordinate adjectives about a work of art.","options":[],"answer":"It's a bold, bright, expressive painting.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses coordinate adjectives (equal, can switch order and add \"and\" → comma) vs cumulative adjectives (in fixed order → no comma); no comma between the last adjective and the noun; adjective order correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spelling Relay","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["Teams line up facing the board.","The teacher says a word; the first student runs to the board and writes the first letter.","The next student adds the next letter, and so on.","The first team with the correct spelling wins the point."],"data":[{"word":"exhibition","clue":"a public show of art or other interesting things"},{"word":"calligraphy","clue":"the art of beautiful handwriting"},{"word":"sculpture","clue":"a piece of art made by shaping stone, wood, metal or clay"},{"word":"masterpiece","clue":"an artist's best and most famous work"},{"word":"imagination","clue":"the ability to create pictures and ideas in your mind"},{"word":"decorative","clue":"beautiful and used to make something look nice"},{"word":"mosaic","clue":"a picture made from many small pieces of colored stone, glass or tile"},{"word":"inspire","clue":"to give someone the wish and ideas to create something"},{"word":"talented","clue":"having a natural ability to do something well"},{"word":"abstract","clue":"using shapes and colors instead of showing real things"},{"word":"landscape","clue":"a painting or photo of an area of land, such as mountains or valleys"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["We watched a funny, clever, play.","We watched a funny clever, play.","We watched a funny, clever play.","We watched, a funny clever play."],"answer":"We watched a funny, clever play.","explanation":"Coordinate adjectives → comma.","explanation_ar":"الصفات المتساوية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["He drives an old white, car.","He drives an old white car.","He drives, an old white car.","He drives an old, white car."],"answer":"He drives an old white car.","explanation":"Cumulative adjectives → no comma.","explanation_ar":"الصفات المتراكمة ← بلا فاصلة."},{"q":"Which phrase needs a comma?","options":["two tall boys","a big green tree","a warm friendly smile","a new leather bag"],"answer":"a warm friendly smile","explanation":"Use the \"switch\" and \"and\" tests.","explanation_ar":"اختبار التبديل وand."},{"q":"","options":["It was a long hot, tiring day.","It was a long, hot, tiring, day.","It was a long, hot, tiring day.","It was, a long hot tiring day."],"answer":"It was a long, hot, tiring day.","explanation":"Coordinate adjectives → comma.","explanation_ar":"الصفات المتساوية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["Grandma gave me three old coins.","Grandma gave me three old, coins.","Grandma gave me three, old coins.","Grandma gave me, three old coins."],"answer":"Grandma gave me three old coins.","explanation":"Cumulative adjectives → no comma.","explanation_ar":"الصفات المتراكمة ← بلا فاصلة."},{"q":"Which phrase has the correct adjective order?","options":["a Turkish lovely small rug","a small lovely Turkish rug","a small Turkish lovely rug","a lovely small Turkish rug"],"answer":"a lovely small Turkish rug","explanation":"Adjective order (opinion – size – age – color – origin – material).","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الصفات."},{"q":"Why is there no comma in \"a small wooden box\"?","options":["The adjectives are coordinate.","The noun is plural.","Both adjectives are colors.","The adjectives are cumulative."],"answer":"The adjectives are cumulative.","explanation":"Cumulative adjectives → no comma.","explanation_ar":"الصفات المتراكمة ← بلا فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["The artist used, soft gentle colors.","The artist used soft, gentle colors.","The artist used soft, gentle, colors.","The artist used soft gentle, colors."],"answer":"The artist used soft, gentle colors.","explanation":"No comma between the last adjective and the noun.","explanation_ar":"لا فاصلة قبل الاسم."},{"q":"Which sentence is punctuated correctly?","options":["The mosque has, tall elegant minarets.","The mosque has tall, elegant, minarets.","The mosque has tall elegant, minarets.","The mosque has tall, elegant minarets."],"answer":"The mosque has tall, elegant minarets.","explanation":"Coordinate adjectives → comma.","explanation_ar":"الصفات المتساوية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"Which test shows that \"brave, kind\" are coordinate adjectives?","options":["\"a kind and brave man\" sounds natural.","Both words are nouns.","\"a brave man kind\" sounds natural.","Both words have four letters."],"answer":"\"a kind and brave man\" sounds natural.","explanation":"Use the \"switch\" and \"and\" tests.","explanation_ar":"اختبار التبديل وand."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Arts and Creativity” that shows coordinate adjectives (equal, can switch order and add \"and\" → comma) vs cumulative adjectives (in fixed order → no comma); no comma between the last adjective and the noun; adjective order in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Arts and Creativity” that shows coordinate adjectives (equal, can switch order and add \"and\" → comma) vs cumulative adjectives (in fixed order → no comma); no comma between the last adjective and the noun; adjective order in action"},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spelling Relay”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spelling Relay"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Bright, Colorful Mosaic: Commas with Coordinate Adjectives”. Let’s learn coordinate adjectives (equal, can switch order and add \"and\" → comma) vs cumulative adjectives (in fixed order → no comma); no comma between the last adjective and the noun; adjective order together. Coordinate adjectives describe a noun equally. Put a comma between them: a bright, colorful mosaic; a long, boring speech. Two tests: (1) Can you switch the order? (a colorful, bright mosaic ✓) (2) Can you put and between them? (a bright and colorful mosaic ✓) If yes, use a comma. Coordinate adjectives describe a noun equally. Put a comma between them: a bright, colorful mosaic; a long, boring speech. Two tests: (1) Can you switch the order? (a colorful, bright mosaic ✓) (2) Can you put and between them? (a bright and colorful mosaic ✓) If yes, use a comma. Cumulative adjectives build on each other in a fixed order (opinion – size – age – shape – color – origin – material – purpose + noun). Don't use a comma: a small wooden box; a beautiful old Persian carpet. The tests fail: (not: a wooden small box), (not: a small and wooden box) (sounds wrong). Here are some examples. It was a bright, colorful mosaic. She bought a small wooden box. The gallery had cool, quiet rooms. Be careful! Some learners say: “It was a bright colorful mosaic.” That’s not right. We say: “It was a bright, colorful mosaic.” Coordinate → comma. Quick check: Can we say \"a colorful and bright mosaic\"? … Think! … Yes – so \"bright, colorful\" needs a comma. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"a bright, colorful mosaic\" with a comma.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS5","title":"A Review of the Young Artists Exhibition: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to discuss an art exhibition and give opinions.","Students will be able to write an exhibition review with the causative, make/let/allow, precise art adjectives and correct commas.","I can talk about an exhibition and my favorite piece.","I can write a short exhibition review."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من مناقشة معرض فني وإبداء آرائهم.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة مراجعة لمعرض بصيغة السببية وmake/let/allow وصفات فنية دقيقة وفواصل صحيحة.","أستطيع أن أتحدث عن معرض وعن قطعتي المفضلة.","أستطيع أن أكتب مراجعة قصيرة لمعرض."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"exhibition","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɛksəˈbɪʃən/","definition":"a public show of art or other interesting things","arabic":"معرض","example":"The school art exhibition opens on Thursday.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"calligraphy","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kəˈlɪɡrəfi/","definition":"the art of beautiful handwriting","arabic":"فن الخط","example":"Arabic calligraphy decorates many mosques.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"sculpture","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈskʌlptʃɚ/","definition":"a piece of art made by shaping stone, wood, metal or clay","arabic":"منحوتة / مجسّم","example":"There's a huge sculpture of a falcon in the square.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"mosaic","pos":"noun","ipa":"/moʊˈzeɪɪk/","definition":"a picture made from many small pieces of colored stone, glass or tile","arabic":"فسيفساء","example":"The mosque floor has a beautiful blue mosaic.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"masterpiece","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmæstɚˌpis/","definition":"an artist's best and most famous work","arabic":"تحفة فنية","example":"This painting is considered a masterpiece.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"inspire","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈspaɪr/","definition":"to give someone the wish and ideas to create something","arabic":"يُلهِم","example":"The desert inspired many of her paintings.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"imagination","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪˌmædʒəˈneɪʃən/","definition":"the ability to create pictures and ideas in your mind","arabic":"خيال","example":"You need a lot of imagination to write stories.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"talented","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈtæləntɪd/","definition":"having a natural ability to do something well","arabic":"موهوب","example":"My cousin is a talented photographer.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"abstract","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/æbˈstrækt/","definition":"using shapes and colors instead of showing real things","arabic":"تجريدي","example":"I don't always understand abstract art.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"landscape","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈlændˌskeɪp/","definition":"a painting or photo of an area of land, such as mountains or valleys","arabic":"منظر طبيعي","example":"He painted a landscape of the Asir mountains.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"gallery","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɡælɚi/","definition":"a building or room where art is shown","arabic":"صالة عرض / معرض فني","example":"We visited a small gallery in Jeddah.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"sketch","pos":"noun","ipa":"/skɛtʃ/","definition":"a quick, simple drawing","arabic":"رسم تخطيطي","example":"She made a sketch before she started painting.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"expressive","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ɪkˈsprɛsɪv/","definition":"showing feelings and meaning clearly","arabic":"معبِّر","example":"Her calligraphy is very expressive.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"decorative","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈdɛkrətɪv/","definition":"beautiful and used to make something look nice","arabic":"زخرفي / تزييني","example":"The box has decorative patterns on the lid.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 6: the causative (had my ticket checked), make / let / allow, art words and adjective suffixes, and commas with coordinate adjectives.\nA review describes what you saw, gives opinions with precise adjectives, mentions interesting details and ends with a recommendation or message.\n✔ have/get + object + past participle\n✔ make/let + person + base verb • allow + person + to\n✔ colorful, expressive, impressive, priceless\n✔ a bright, peaceful gallery (comma) • a small wooden frame (no comma)","examples":["I had my photo taken next to the giant sculpture.","The gallery didn't allow visitors to touch the artwork.","The guide let us ask the artists questions.","The calligraphy was elegant and expressive.","It was a quiet, thoughtful exhibition.","The mosaics were truly impressive.","Each artist had his work framed professionally.","I recommend the exhibition to anyone with imagination."],"common_errors":["✗ I had checked my ticket at the door. (someone checked it) → ✓ I had my ticket checked at the door. (Causative word order.)","✗ The teacher made him to start again. → ✓ The teacher made him start again. (make + base verb.)","✗ It was a large colorful mosaic. → ✓ It was a large, colorful mosaic. (Coordinate adjectives → comma.)"],"arabic":"نراجع صيغة السببية وmake/let/allow وكلمات الفن ولواحق الصفات والفواصل بين الصفات المتساوية.\nالمراجعة تصف ما رأيته وتعطي رأيك بصفات دقيقة وتذكر تفاصيل ممتعة وتنتهي بتوصية.\nتذكّر: had my ticket checked، وmade him start (دون to)، وa bright, peaceful gallery."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Review of the Young Artists Exhibition: Language in Use”. Let’s learn causative have/get, make/let/allow, art words and adjective suffixes, commas with coordinate adjectives (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L07-U6-LS5 | A Review of the Young Artists Exhibition: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Gallery critics: in groups, choose three pieces of art (from the classroom display or pictures). Describe each with coordinate adjectives, give one rule of the gallery (allowed / not allowed) and one thing the organizers had done. Then vote for the best piece and explain why.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 6: the causative (had my ticket checked), make / let / allow, art words and adjective suffixes, and commas with coordinate adjectives. A review describes what you saw, gives opinions with precise adjectives, mentions interesting details and ends with a recommendation or message.","on_screen":"✔ have/get + object + past participle • ✔ make/let + person + base verb • allow + person + to • ✔ colorful, expressive, impressive, priceless","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I had my photo taken next to the giant sculpture. The gallery didn't allow visitors to touch the artwork. The guide let us ask the artists questions.","on_screen":"I had my photo taken next to the giant sculpture. / The gallery didn't allow visitors to touch the artwork. / The guide let us ask the artists questions.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I had checked my ticket at the door. (someone checked it).” That’s not right. We say: “I had my ticket checked at the door.” Causative word order.","on_screen":"✗ I had checked my ticket at the door. (someone checked it)   ✓ I had my ticket checked at the door.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “The teacher made him to start again.”? … Think! … It should be “The teacher made him start again.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can talk about an exhibition and my favorite piece.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can talk about an exhibition and my favorite piece.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: causative have/get, make/let/allow, art words and adjective suffixes, commas with coordinate adjectives (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع صيغة السببية وmake/let/allow وكلمات الفن ولواحق الصفات والفواصل بين الصفات المتساوية.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I had checked my ticket at the door. (someone checked it) — الصحيح: I had my ticket checked at the door.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أتحدث عن معرض وعن قطعتي المفضلة."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Young Artists of Taif – A Review by Omar","body":"Last Thursday, I had my ticket checked at the door of the \"Young Artists of Taif\" exhibition, and I walked into a bright, peaceful gallery.\nThe organizers had let every student choose his own theme, so the artwork was wonderfully varied.\nThe most impressive piece was a large, colorful mosaic of a desert sunset.\nIts young artist told me that his teacher had made him start again three times!\nIn the next room, there were delicate, expressive sketches of old Taif houses.\nI also had my name written in calligraphy by a talented calligrapher, which was a lovely surprise.\nThe exhibition showed me that imagination is priceless.","word_count":107,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Omar's review. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Omar visited the exhibition last Thursday.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Young Artists of Taif – A Review by Omar”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The organizers chose one theme for all the students.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Young Artists of Taif – A Review by Omar”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The most impressive piece was a mosaic of a desert sunset.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Young Artists of Taif – A Review by Omar”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The young artist got it right the first time.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Young Artists of Taif – A Review by Omar”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"There were sketches of old Taif houses.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Young Artists of Taif – A Review by Omar”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Omar wrote his own name in calligraphy.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Young Artists of Taif – A Review by Omar”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Omar ___ his ticket checked at the door.","options":["made","let","did","had"],"answer":"had","explanation":"Causative have/get something done.","explanation_ar":"صيغة السببية."},{"q":"The organizers let every student ___ his own theme.","options":["choose","chose","to choose","choosing"],"answer":"choose","explanation":"make / let / allow.","explanation_ar":"make وlet وallow."},{"q":"His teacher had made him ___ again three times.","options":["starting","started","start","to start"],"answer":"start","explanation":"make / let / allow.","explanation_ar":"make وlet وallow."},{"q":"The mosaic was the most ___ piece.","options":["impress","impression","impressive","impressively"],"answer":"impressive","explanation":"Art word or adjective suffix.","explanation_ar":"كلمة فنية أو لاحقة."},{"q":"","options":["There were delicate, expressive, sketches.","There were delicate, expressive sketches.","There were, delicate expressive sketches.","There were delicate expressive, sketches."],"answer":"There were delicate, expressive sketches.","explanation":"Commas with coordinate adjectives.","explanation_ar":"فواصل الصفات."},{"q":"\"Imagination is priceless\" means imagination is ___.","options":["worth nothing","easy to buy","very cheap","extremely valuable"],"answer":"extremely valuable","explanation":"Art word or adjective suffix.","explanation_ar":"كلمة فنية أو لاحقة."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Be a gallery critic. Write your notes.","items":[{"q":"Piece 1: describe it with two coordinate adjectives.","options":[],"answer":"a bold, colorful painting of a falcon","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses causative have/get, make/let/allow, art words and adjective suffixes, commas with coordinate adjectives (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Piece 2: describe it with an adjective with a suffix.","options":[],"answer":"an expressive calligraphy panel","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses causative have/get, make/let/allow, art words and adjective suffixes, commas with coordinate adjectives (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A gallery rule with allowed / not allowed: ___","options":[],"answer":"Visitors aren't allowed to use flash.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses causative have/get, make/let/allow, art words and adjective suffixes, commas with coordinate adjectives (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something the organizers had done: ___","options":[],"answer":"They had the paintings framed in gold.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses causative have/get, make/let/allow, art words and adjective suffixes, commas with coordinate adjectives (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Your vote and reason: ___","options":[],"answer":"I vote for the falcon painting because it's full of energy.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses causative have/get, make/let/allow, art words and adjective suffixes, commas with coordinate adjectives (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your review.","items":[{"q":"Plan: name of the exhibition, the gallery, 2–3 pieces, a rule, a causative, your opinion.","options":[],"answer":"Art of the Desert; small, bright gallery; mosaic of camels, abstract painting, sculpture of a palm tree; no photos allowed; had my portfolio signed by an artist; inspiring","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses causative have/get, make/let/allow, art words and adjective suffixes, commas with coordinate adjectives (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your review in 7–8 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"Last week, I visited \"Art of the Desert\" in a small, bright gallery in Jeddah. Visitors weren't allowed to take photos, so I looked carefully at every piece. The most impressive work was a huge mosaic of camels crossing the dunes. There was also a mysterious abstract painting that made me think. A talented sculptor let us watch him carve a palm tree from wood. I had my sketchbook signed by one of the artists. The exhibition was colorful, creative and inspiring. I recommend it to everyone.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses causative have/get, make/let/allow, art words and adjective suffixes, commas with coordinate adjectives (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: causative word order? make/let + base verb? commas with coordinate adjectives? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"a small bright gallery\" to \"a small, bright gallery\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses causative have/get, make/let/allow, art words and adjective suffixes, commas with coordinate adjectives (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Board Race Review","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["One student from each team stands at the board.","The teacher says a cue word and a task (meaning, spelling or sentence with causative have/get, make/let/allow, art words and adjective suffixes, commas with coordinate adjectives (unit review)).","The first correct answer wins a point; rotate players every round.","Play 10 rounds."],"data":[{"cue":"exhibition","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"calligraphy","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"sculpture","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"mosaic","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"masterpiece","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"inspire","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"imagination","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"talented","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"abstract","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"landscape","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"gallery","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"sketch","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"expressive","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"decorative","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Before the exhibition, we ___ all the paintings photographed.","options":["made","did","let","had"],"answer":"had","explanation":"Causative have/get something done.","explanation_ar":"صيغة السببية."},{"q":"I'm getting my calligraphy ___ for my grandfather's birthday.","options":["framing","to frame","framed","frame"],"answer":"framed","explanation":"Causative have/get something done.","explanation_ar":"صيغة السببية."},{"q":"The gallery doesn't ___ children under ten to enter alone.","options":["have","allow","let","make"],"answer":"allow","explanation":"make / let / allow.","explanation_ar":"make وlet وallow."},{"q":"My art teacher ___ me use her special brushes.","options":["let to","made to","allowed","let"],"answer":"let","explanation":"make / let / allow.","explanation_ar":"make وlet وallow."},{"q":"We were made ___ our names on every drawing.","options":["write","to write","writing","written"],"answer":"to write","explanation":"make / let / allow.","explanation_ar":"make وlet وallow."},{"q":"The sculptor is famous for his ___ work.","options":["imaginative","imagine","imaginatively","imagination"],"answer":"imaginative","explanation":"Art word or adjective suffix.","explanation_ar":"كلمة فنية أو لاحقة."},{"q":"","options":["It was a quiet, elegant, gallery.","It was a quiet elegant, gallery.","It was, a quiet elegant gallery.","It was a quiet, elegant gallery."],"answer":"It was a quiet, elegant gallery.","explanation":"Commas with coordinate adjectives.","explanation_ar":"فواصل الصفات."},{"q":"","options":["She showed us, two beautiful blue vases.","She showed us two beautiful, blue, vases.","She showed us two beautiful blue vases.","She showed us two, beautiful blue vases."],"answer":"She showed us two beautiful blue vases.","explanation":"Commas with coordinate adjectives.","explanation_ar":"فواصل الصفات."},{"q":"Her ___ of the old souq was used on the school calendar.","options":["sketcher","sketched","sketch","sketchy"],"answer":"sketch","explanation":"Art word or adjective suffix.","explanation_ar":"كلمة فنية أو لاحقة."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for an exhibition review:","options":["The organizers had the walls painted white, which made the bright, colorful paintings stand out.","The organizers had painted the walls white by painters, which made the bright colorful, paintings stand out.","The organizers made the walls to be painted white, which made the bright colorful paintings stand out.","The organizers had the walls paint white, which made the bright, colorful, paintings stand out."],"answer":"The organizers had the walls painted white, which made the bright, colorful paintings stand out.","explanation":"Causative have/get something done.","explanation_ar":"صيغة السببية."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"The \"Young Artists of Taif\" exhibition: a large colorful mosaic of a desert sunset, delicate sketches of old Taif houses, a calligrapher writing visitors' names; Omar holding a notebook and writing his review. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"The \"Young Artists of Taif\" exhibition: a large colorful mosaic of a desert sunset, delicate sketches of old Taif houses, a calligrapher writing visitors' names; Omar holding a notebook and writing his review"},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Arts and Creativity”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Arts and Creativity”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L07-U6-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Board Race Review”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Board Race Review"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS5-T1","script":"Last Thursday, I had my ticket checked at the door of the \"Young Artists of Taif\" exhibition, and I walked into a bright, peaceful gallery. The organizers had let every student choose his own theme, so the artwork was wonderfully varied. The most impressive piece was a large, colorful mosaic of a desert sunset. Its young artist told me that his teacher had made him start again three times! In the next room, there were delicate, expressive sketches of old Taif houses. I also had my name written in calligraphy by a talented calligrapher, which was a lovely surprise. The exhibition showed me that imagination is priceless.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"1.0"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L07-U6-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Review of the Young Artists Exhibition: Language in Use”. Let’s learn causative have/get, make/let/allow, art words and adjective suffixes, commas with coordinate adjectives (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Gallery critics: in groups, choose three pieces of art (from the classroom display or pictures). Describe each with coordinate adjectives, give one rule of the gallery (allowed / not allowed) and one thing the organizers had done. Then vote for the best piece and explain why. Today you use all of Unit 6: the causative (had my ticket checked), make / let / allow, art words and adjective suffixes, and commas with coordinate adjectives. A review describes what you saw, gives opinions with precise adjectives, mentions interesting details and ends with a recommendation or message. Here are some examples. I had my photo taken next to the giant sculpture. The gallery didn't allow visitors to touch the artwork. The guide let us ask the artists questions. Be careful! Some learners say: “I had checked my ticket at the door. (someone checked it).” That’s not right. We say: “I had my ticket checked at the door.” Causative word order. Quick check: what is wrong with “The teacher made him to start again.”? … Think! … It should be “The teacher made him start again.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can talk about an exhibition and my favorite piece.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"1.0"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"I don't repair my own phone. I ___ it repaired at a shop.","options":["make","have","let","do"],"answer":"have","explanation":"have + object + past participle.","explanation_ar":"have + المفعول + التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"We got the invitations ___ at a print shop.","options":["printing","print","to print","printed"],"answer":"printed","explanation":"get + object + past participle (informal).","explanation_ar":"get للتعبير غير الرسمي."},{"q":"My grandparents are ___ their old house restored this year.","options":["making","letting","having","doing"],"answer":"having","explanation":"Change the tense of have/get.","explanation_ar":"زمن have/get."},{"q":"The coach had the players ___ the field after the match.","options":["cleaning","cleaned","to clean","clean"],"answer":"clean","explanation":"have + person + base verb.","explanation_ar":"have + الشخص + المصدر."},{"q":"A tailor shortened Ziyad's thobe for him. Which sentence says this?","options":["Ziyad shortened his thobe himself.","Ziyad had shortened his thobe.","Ziyad had his thobe shorten.","Ziyad had his thobe shortened."],"answer":"Ziyad had his thobe shortened.","explanation":"Object before the past participle.","explanation_ar":"المفعول قبل التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"","options":["The museum had its windows replace last year.","The museum had its windows replaced last year.","The museum had its windows to be replaced last year.","The museum had replaced its windows by workers last year."],"answer":"The museum had its windows replaced last year.","explanation":"have + object + past participle.","explanation_ar":"have + المفعول + التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"My teacher makes us ___ our work twice.","options":["to check","checked","check","checking"],"answer":"check","explanation":"make + person + base verb (force).","explanation_ar":"make للإجبار."},{"q":"Will your parents let you ___ to the exhibition alone?","options":["to go","go","went","going"],"answer":"go","explanation":"let + person + base verb (permission).","explanation_ar":"let للإذن."},{"q":"Visitors are not allowed ___ food into the gallery.","options":["brought","to bring","bringing","bring"],"answer":"to bring","explanation":"allow + person + to + verb.","explanation_ar":"allow مع to."},{"q":"","options":["We were made wear safety glasses in the workshop.","We were let to wear safety glasses in the workshop.","We were made to wear safety glasses in the workshop.","We made to wear safety glasses in the workshop."],"answer":"We were made to wear safety glasses in the workshop.","explanation":"be made to / be allowed to (no passive with let).","explanation_ar":"المبني للمجهول."},{"q":"\"The guard didn't let us take photos.\" What does this mean?","options":["The guard took photos of us.","We took many photos.","We were forced to take photos.","We weren't allowed to take photos."],"answer":"We weren't allowed to take photos.","explanation":"let + person + base verb (permission).","explanation_ar":"let للإذن."},{"q":"The old painting is ___. Even a museum couldn't buy it.","options":["careless","pointless","worthless","priceless"],"answer":"priceless","explanation":"Tricky meanings (priceless vs worthless).","explanation_ar":"المعنى الدقيق."},{"q":"She used many bright colors. Her painting is ___.","options":["colorly","colorless","colorful","colorist"],"answer":"colorful","explanation":"Choose the right suffix (-ful, -less, -ous, -ive).","explanation_ar":"اللاحقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"The Hijazi houses have ___ wooden windows called rawashin.","options":["decorative","decoration","decorate","decoratively"],"answer":"decorative","explanation":"Choose the right word-family form.","explanation_ar":"الصيغة الصحيحة."},{"q":"An artist's best and most famous work is a ___.","options":["masterpiece","landscape","sketch","gallery"],"answer":"masterpiece","explanation":"Choose the art word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"Art that uses shapes and colors instead of real things is ___.","options":["talented","abstract","expressive","decorative"],"answer":"abstract","explanation":"Choose the art word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى."},{"q":"The story had a strange, ___ ending that nobody understood.","options":["mysteriously","mysterious","mysterial","mystery"],"answer":"mysterious","explanation":"Choose the right suffix (-ful, -less, -ous, -ive).","explanation_ar":"اللاحقة الصحيحة."},{"q":"","options":["It was a long, exciting, journey.","It was a long exciting, journey.","It was a long, exciting journey.","It was, a long exciting journey."],"answer":"It was a long, exciting journey.","explanation":"Coordinate adjectives → comma.","explanation_ar":"الصفات المتساوية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["My brother has a new leather wallet.","My brother has, a new leather wallet.","My brother has a new, leather wallet.","My brother has a new leather, wallet."],"answer":"My brother has a new leather wallet.","explanation":"Cumulative adjectives → no comma.","explanation_ar":"الصفات المتراكمة ← بلا فاصلة."},{"q":"In which phrase should a comma separate the adjectives?","options":["a gentle quiet voice","three small rooms","a red plastic bag","an old stone bridge"],"answer":"a gentle quiet voice","explanation":"Use the \"switch\" and \"and\" tests.","explanation_ar":"اختبار التبديل وand."},{"q":"Choose the phrase with natural adjective order.","options":["a big nice old house","an old nice big house","a nice big old house","an old big nice house"],"answer":"a nice big old house","explanation":"Object before the past participle.","explanation_ar":"المفعول قبل التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"Which sentence would fit best in an exhibition review?","options":["I had my program signed by a talented, friendly artist, who let me watch him paint.","I had my program sign by a talented, friendly, artist, who let me watch him paint.","I had signed my program by a talented friendly, artist, who let me to watch him paint.","I had my program signed by a talented friendly artist who made me to watch him paint."],"answer":"I had my program signed by a talented, friendly artist, who let me watch him paint.","explanation":"Coordinate adjectives → comma.","explanation_ar":"الصفات المتساوية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"the teacher made us to clean the bright colorful brushes.\"","options":["The teacher made us clean the bright, colorful brushes.","The teacher made us to clean the bright, colorful brushes.","The teacher made us clean the bright colorful brushes.","the teacher made us clean the bright, colorful brushes."],"answer":"The teacher made us clean the bright, colorful brushes.","explanation":"make + person + base verb (force).","explanation_ar":"make للإجبار."},{"q":"\"I'm having my artwork scanned.\" Who is scanning the artwork?","options":["I am","Nobody","My artwork","Someone else"],"answer":"Someone else","explanation":"have + object + past participle.","explanation_ar":"have + المفعول + التصريف الثالث."}],"theme_ar":"الفنون والإبداع","essential_question_ar":"لماذا يبدع الناس الفن؟","can_do":"I can talk about services with have/get something done, describe rules and permission with make, let and allow, use art words and adjective suffixes, and punctuate coordinate adjectives correctly.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أتحدث عن الخدمات بـ have/get something done، وأصف القواعد والإذن بـ make وlet وallow، وأستخدم كلمات الفن ولواحق الصفات، وأضع الفواصل بين الصفات المتساوية بشكل صحيح."});
